    "q-138579": {
      "dom_id": "step-q138579",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n{U}_{r}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{Σ}_{r}=[\\begin{aligned}5\\end{aligned}],\\,{V}_{r}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}_{r}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of ${Σ}_{r}.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\n{Σ}_{r}^{+}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1\\end{aligned}],\\,{U}_{r}^{T}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & ={V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-138579-a",
